diff --git a/docs/reviews.md b/docs/reviews.md
index 88ac479..5cbd371 100644
--- a/docs/reviews.md
+++ b/docs/reviews.md
@@ -247,3 +247,19 @@ Observations (non-blocking):
 Concurrent session note (out of scope, flagged for escalation): scripts/engine/weather_state.py ports the deleted seven state ladder as a Python twin with weather_state_goldens.json, public/data/engine/atlas.json ships a 77 district seven state cartogram, and build.py plus verify.py (258 new lines; the drift gate now asserts atlas invariants) were edited to emit and check it. (a) No E6 file imports or depends on any of it (grep: zero references in judgeMode, rehearsal, judge/, ConsoleView, consoleStore). (b) Nothing breaks as it stands: vitest 527 green, pytest 170 green (the 10 new tests are all in scripts/engine/test_atlas.py, 8 atlas plus 2 weather_state golden tests), and scripts.engine.verify passes with the profiles.json sha256 9ec428bf... unchanged. (c) Risk: the seven state vocabulary now lives in two languages with its own goldens and a district shading surface, contradicting the user confirmed single vocabulary decision (verdict.ts owns every band; the E5 record forbids reintroducing the ladder) and the freshly fixed README; the verify gate is now coupled to atlas.json invariants, so reverting the ladder under time pressure means editing verify.py before the findings freeze, and the decisions.md entry is filed as Phase E5 which will confuse provenance at judging time. Escalate to the user: accept the twin as an approved amendment (updating the E5 record and README to match) or revert weather_state.py, atlas.json, and the atlas build and verify hooks before the findings freeze; do not let E7 land on top of the ambiguity.

 Recurring patterns for other agents: the single registry plus comment only store discipline from earlier phases held; watch the dash gate coverage when adding new component directories.
+
+## Nov 08 2026, Phase E7: Solana A+ touch review (chain receipt registry, receipt stamp, bundled memo evidence)
+
+Verdict: PASS (3 Low notes, 0 Medium or higher; all ten contract checks verified; suites green: npx vitest run 53 files / 589 tests passed, npm run typecheck clean with zero errors, npm run build PASS 80 modules, uv run pytest 184 passed, uv run python -m scripts.engine.verify PASS with profiles.json sha256 9ec428bf1a78b35703aa3d36311d4ee061eac7fbd1176cfcbf111acc5c40a858; independent shasum confirms all three receipt payload digests byte exact)
+
+| Severity | File:Line | Issue | Fix |
+|----------|-----------|-------|-----|
+| Low | src/data/receipts.test.ts:121 to 128 | The model card digest test early returns when the receipt is absent (lines 123 to 126), so a parseChainReceipt regression that drops the receipt would skip the digest pin silently; the registry test at lines 141 to 154 only catches files missing from disk, not parse failures masquerading as absence | Assert the modelcard receipt exists (fail instead of returning), or pin loadBundledReceipts length to the on disk file count so a dropped receipt cannot hide |
+| Low | src/data/receipts.test.ts | No test pins the fingerprint receipt digest to build/f1-aggregate-table.json (that source is a generated artifact outside public/data, unlike root and modelcard); this review verified it by shasum (84f5f24be8f1c74e3ca645fdebfd0f41e52f916c0cc84f6059ada2554138cccd matches the evidence), but a regenerated artifact could drift untested | Add a conditional digest assertion for the fingerprint when build/f1-aggregate-table.json exists, mirroring the modelcard case |
+| Low | workspace (no .git) | The checkout has no git history, so ReceiptBadge byte identity (judge/ diff empty), the BaselineCard seam diff, and the index.css appended block boundary were verified by inspection and pinned tests only, never by git diff | None possible in this checkout; the wording is pinned by ReceiptBadge.test.ts and the seam behavior by ReceiptStamp.test.ts |
+
+Verified clean: zero runtime network (receipts.ts reads the bundled evidence through import.meta.glob eager at lines 110 to 113, no fetch, XMLHttpRequest, RPC, or web3 call anywhere in receipts.ts or ReceiptStamp.tsx; the only network affordances are plain anchors to the bundled evidence file via dataBase() and to the explorer); the three public/data/memo-devnet files are field for field identical to their scripts/solana/evidence siblings and the signatures match the reported devnet transactions (root 5YPxwK9, modelcard 3BJiraS5t, fingerprint Q7evLcRbo); honesty copy exact (the zero receipt placeholder renders the pinned "no evidence yet" badge with zero rows, no explorer anchor, and no "Anchored at build time" note, ReceiptStamp.tsx lines 38 to 39 and 88 pinned at ReceiptStamp.test.ts 107 to 116); badge wording is the docs/solana.md contract verbatim (docs/solana.md 122 and 126 against ReceiptBadge.tsx 51, 54, 60, pinned at ReceiptBadge.test.ts 25 to 52); anchor titles honest (EVIDENCE_TITLE and EXPLORER_TITLE describe exactly where each link goes); no em dash, en dash, minus sign, or spaced hyphen in any new string (independent grep over src, public/data, and scripts/solana clean; the remaining spaced hyphens in E7 files are code arithmetic only at receipts.ts 128, receipts.test.ts 153, ReceiptStamp.test.ts 70; receipts.test.ts 156 to 179 adds its own runtime dash gate; dashScan green inside vitest with receipts.ts and receipts.test.ts registered at dashScan.test.ts 35 to 36 and asserted at 193 to 198, console dir auto scan covers the ReceiptStamp pair, index.css in CSS_FILES); scope lock holds (no wallet UI, no Anchor framework, no tokens, no runtime RPC in the diff); index.css E7 block is contiguous at the file tail (comment at 2591 through EOF at 2634, all five cp-receipt rules at 2593 to 2634 and no cp-receipt reference earlier in the file); digest gate: shasum 256 of public/data/findings.json equals 48bb57a409459812ae2bfead9ae688bf5d38b4c4786dabf15e1e05d52b8b3bc3, of public/data/model_card.json equals b3b32f0c0f284c3cac2e3df6e7d680fc53a5313b206750053f838853b9a0efe3, and of build/f1-aggregate-table.json equals 84f5f24be8f1c74e3ca645fdebfd0f41e52f916c0cc84f6059ada2554138cccd, all matching the bundled evidence payload_sha256 fields exactly; send timestamps noted (root confirmed 2026-11-07T02:47:12Z slot 519514224, modelcard 2026-11-08T06:43:55Z slot 519934572, fingerprint 2026-11-08T06:44:11Z slot 519934638, both later sends before the Sun 12 PM submit hard stop and pinning bytes that still match the current artifacts).
+
+Suite count notes: vitest reports 53 files / 589 tests versus the phase brief snapshot of 51 files / 564 tests (the concurrent atlas session grew its test set between the snapshot and this run; 100 percent green, no failures). npm run typecheck is now clean with zero errors anywhere, so the AGENTS.md routing note about 12 TS2532 and TS2345 errors in src/lib/atlasData.test.ts is stale as of this run; attribution confirmed zero errors in E7 files and zero overall.
+
+Recurring patterns: the test that guards a contract should not skip when the guarded artifact disappears (the modelcard early return is the skip pattern first seen as conditional raw CSV tests in Phase E3), and generated artifacts pinned by digest need at least one test or gate that recomputes the digest (only root and modelcard are pinned in tests today).
